1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,954
Ask smart people to fix a

2
00:00:01,954 --> 00:00:03,440
wobbly Lego bridge,

3
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:05,081
a cluttered schedule,

4
00:00:05,081 --> 00:00:06,645
or a bloated budget,

5
00:00:06,645 --> 00:00:08,990
and almost everyone adds more.

6
00:00:08,990 --> 00:00:11,676
Across eight experiments published in Nature

7
00:00:11,676 --> 00:00:12,164
in 2021,

8
00:00:12,164 --> 00:00:13,141
Gabrielle Adams,

9
00:00:13,141 --> 00:00:13,874
Leidy Klotz,

10
00:00:13,874 --> 00:00:16,987
and colleagues found humans systematically overlook

11
00:00:16,987 --> 00:00:18,208
subtractive changes,

12
00:00:18,208 --> 00:00:20,100
even when removing one piece is

13
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:21,260
faster and cheaper.

14
00:00:21,260 --> 00:00:22,677
Under mental overload,

15
00:00:22,677 --> 00:00:24,609
that additive bias gets worse:

16
00:00:24,609 --> 00:00:26,799
we pile new productivity apps onto

17
00:00:26,799 --> 00:00:29,247
broken routines and stack side hustles

18
00:00:29,247 --> 00:00:31,050
onto leaky monthly overhead.

19
00:00:31,050 --> 00:00:33,702
Adopt Nassim Taleb's Via Negativa rule:

20
00:00:33,702 --> 00:00:35,606
before adding any new habit,

21
00:00:35,606 --> 00:00:35,946
tool,

22
00:00:35,946 --> 00:00:36,694
or expense,

23
00:00:36,694 --> 00:00:39,346
delete one recurring obligation or bill

24
00:00:39,346 --> 00:00:41,590
that drains your baseline energy.

25
00:00:41,590 --> 00:00:43,107
Subtract friction first,

26
00:00:43,107 --> 00:00:45,383
and your existing focus and cashflow

27
00:00:45,383 --> 00:00:47,911
start compounding without a single extra

28
00:00:47,911 --> 00:00:48,670
moving part.
